# What the build does not need, and what it must not carry.
#
# The context is sent to the daemon before anything is built, so this is the
# last point at which a deployment's own files can be kept out of an image
# that is going to be pushed somewhere public.

# A deployment. None of this belongs in an image, and a log or a database
# from the machine that built it is the clearest example of why.
*.log
*.db
*.db-*
.jingclaw/

# Built here, built again inside. A binary from the host is the wrong
# architecture as often as not.
core/bin/
build/

# History, and the largest thing in the directory.
.git/
.github/

# Not read by the build, and one of them is personal.
.claude/
.DS_Store
docs/research/
fixtures/
macos/
scripts/
JINGCLAW.md
